/// This is copied from Cargokit (which is the official way to use it currently)
/// Details: https://fzyzcjy.github.io/flutter_rust_bridge/manual/integrate/builtin

Experimental repository to provide glue for seamlessly integrating cargo build
with flutter plugins and packages.

See https://matejknopp.com/post/flutter_plugin_in_rust_with_no_prebuilt_binaries/
for a tutorial on how to use Cargokit.

Example plugin available at https://github.com/irondash/hello_rust_ffi_plugin.

LOCAL CHANGES (mydia)
---------------------

This directory is a vendored copy of Cargokit. It has been modified. If you
re-vendor it from upstream, reapply the following (all tagged in-file with
`LOCAL CHANGE (mydia, #252)`):

  build_tool/lib/src/rust_toolchain_file.dart
      New file. Resolves `[toolchain] channel` from the nearest
      rust-toolchain.toml.

  build_tool/lib/src/builder.dart
      `_toolchain` consults the repo pin between the cargokit_options.yaml
      opt-in and upstream's 'stable' fallback. `build()` invokes `cargo` from
      PATH with RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN set, falling back to `rustup run` only when
      PATH has no cargo. Adds cargoOnPath() and buildsThroughRustup().

  build_tool/lib/src/artifacts_provider.dart
      Constructs Rustup() and calls prepare() only when the build actually
      goes through rustup.

  build_tool/lib/src/rustup.dart
      The `nonCustom` toolchain-list filter also accepts version-numbered
      toolchains.

  build_tool/test/rust_toolchain_file_test.dart
      New file. Unit tests for the resolver. Run with `dart run`, not
      `dart test`; see the note at the top of that file.

Why: upstream builds with `rustup run stable`, which is an explicit toolchain
name and overrides every pinning mechanism, so the Rust compiler behind every
shipped native library was host state rather than a declared version. See
https://github.com/getmydia/mydia/issues/252.

Why RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN rather than `rustup run <pin>`: naming the toolchain to
`rustup run` forces rustup's own dynamically linked binaries, which fail under
the Gradle daemon on NixOS with "libz.so.1: cannot open shared object file".
Setting RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN instead lets a Nix-provided cargo win locally while
rustup's proxies still honour the pin (and auto-install it) in CI and Docker.

